From 4b2c5bf0ebc327c478c348364c2f0996d3ee60cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ironydelerium <42721860+ironydelerium@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Dec 2021 02:20:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Reintroduce TelephonyMetrics stub for MediaTek IMS
 compatibility

The MediaTek IMS package invokes several TelephonyMetrics methods via the
singleton TelephonyMetrics.getInstance():
  - writeRilSendSms(int, int, int, int)
  - writeOnRilSolicitedResponse(int, int, int, int, Object)
  - writeOnRilTimeoutResponse(int, int, int)
  - writeRilAnswer(int, int, int, int)

Google removed the entire TelephonyMetrics class in android-16.0.0_r4,
replacing it with individual stats classes. MediaTek vendor blobs still
reference the old class, causing NoSuchMethodError crashes in
com.mediatek.ims (specifically in ImsRILAdapter.processResponseDoneInternal).

This patch creates a minimal stub TelephonyMetrics class with no-op
implementations of all methods that MTK IMS blobs call.

Fixes https://github.com/phhusson/treble_experimentations/issues/2125.

Co-authored-by: Sarah Vandomelen <sarah@sightworks.com>
---
 .../telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java   | 68 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 68 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..1234567890
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
